##

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.560 line:91%
This is Alec Steele,
blacksmith, YouTuber.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.000 line:85%
You make all sorts of stuff.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.880 line:91%
I brought some cameras,
we're going to make a thing.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.760 line:91%
I don't really know what's
going to happen now.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.710 line:91%
<c.yellow>Well, we're going to
make a bottle opener.</c>

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.543 line:85%
Yep.

00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:13.790 line:85%
<c.yellow>But what we're also going to do,</c>

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.240 position:61% line:91%
is we are going to make the tools
that we need to make the bottle opener.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.073 line:85%
Right.

00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:19.619 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>'Cos that's one of the special things
about blacksmithing,</c>

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.865 line:91%
<c.yellow>is the blacksmith was
one of the only craftsmen</c>

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:24.740 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>that literally could make pretty much
all the tools in his workshop</c>

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.670 line:85%
<c.yellow>to make all the items that somebody</c>

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.060 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>would actually want to buy from him.</c>

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.300 line:85%
Huh.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.240 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's relatively basic.</c>

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.860 line:91%
<c.yellow>I think it's going to be a
little bit of a challenge.</c>

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.083 line:91%
Okay
<c.yellow>There's a lot to learn.</c>

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:33.916 line:85%
It is for me!

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.410 line:85%
I've never done anything like this.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.970 line:85%
I don't even know where to start.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.210 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>So, we're going to get the forge lit,</c>

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.050 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm going to tell you how to
hopefully not burn yourself.</c>

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:41.904 line:85%
Yep.

00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:42.737 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>And then, we're going to start forging</c>

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:43.840 line:85%
<c.yellow>a point for the drift</c>

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.340 line:91%
<c.yellow>that you're going to make
while I make a punch.</c>

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.173 line:85%
Right.

00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:48.880 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>And they're needed to make ourselves</c>

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.500 line:85%
<c.yellow>this beverage opening device.</c>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.020 line:85%
What's a drift? <i>(laughs)</i>

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.020 line:85%
<c.yellow>...we'll get to that.</c>

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.223 line:85%
<c.yellow>3, 2, 1.</c>

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:02.472 line:85%
<i>(hoots)</i>

00:01:04.244 --> 00:01:06.990 line:91%
Thank you for moving the
camera out just in time there.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:07.894 line:85%
Wow.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.347 line:91%
<c.yellow>So these are the tools that
we're going to be making.</c>

00:01:11.347 --> 00:01:12.700 line:85%
All right, okay.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.820 line:85%
<c.yellow>This is a slot punch.</c>

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:15.653 line:85%
Yep.

00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:18.400 line:91%
<c.yellow>It makes a hole that
is shaped like a slot.</c>

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.273 line:85%
All right, yep.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.780 line:85%
<c.yellow>This is a drift.</c>

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.261 line:85%
<c.yellow>And, the profile of this means that</c>

00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:27.426 line:85%
<c.yellow>you take a rectangular slot,</c>

00:01:27.426 --> 00:01:29.027 line:91%
<c.yellow>and you push it through
the material,</c>

00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:31.556 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then you gradually enlarge
it into a round hole.</c>

00:01:31.556 --> 00:01:32.389 line:85%
Okay.

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:33.861 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, a punch makes the hole,</c>

00:01:33.861 --> 00:01:36.370 line:91%
<c.yellow>a drift "drifts"
or enlarges it open.</c>

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.420 line:85%
All right.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.020 line:85%
<c.yellow>For us to make both of these,</c>

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.470 line:91%
<c.yellow>we're going to need to do
one of the most</c>

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.370 line:91%
<c.yellow>critical and key parts
of blacksmithing,</c>

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.000 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>which is forging a taper or a point.</c>

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.833 line:85%
Right.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:51.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>So, it's changing the cross-section
of the material by displacing it,</c>

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.970 line:85%
<c.yellow>making it thinner as we go.</c>

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.178 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, that's a taper.</c>

00:01:55.178 --> 00:01:56.011 line:85%
Yep.

00:01:56.011 --> 00:01:57.180 line:91%
<c.yellow>And, what'll happen is,
is we'll start</c>

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.060 line:85%
<c.yellow>with a bar that looks like this,</c>

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.300 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>and all of that material right there</c>

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.588 line:91%
<c.yellow>is going to be shoved
out there like Play-Doh.</c>

00:02:03.588 --> 00:02:04.421 line:85%
Okay.

00:02:04.421 --> 00:02:08.980 line:91%
<c.yellow>Forging is that, it is
displacing this plastic material.</c>

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.600 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>So, I'm going to demonstrate each heat</c>

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.710 line:85%
<c.yellow>and then you'll do the same.</c>

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.543 line:85%
Okay.

00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:16.200 line:85%
<c.yellow>Oh, sorry, a heat is every instance</c>

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.558 position:63% line:85%
<c.yellow>of taking the material out to the anvil.</c>

00:02:18.558 --> 00:02:19.391 line:85%
Uh-huh.

00:02:19.391 --> 00:02:20.360 position:61% line:85%
<c.yellow>Every time that comes out to the anvil,</c>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.580 line:85%
<c.yellow>we are taking a heat.</c>

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.920 size:72% position:64% line:85%
<c.yellow>Here we go, so.</c>

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.753 size:75% position:63% line:85%
Yep.

00:02:23.753 --> 00:02:25.450 size:72% position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>Like I said, about a
30 degree angle here.</c>

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.283 size:75% position:63% line:85%
Yep.

00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:28.490 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>You're going to tilt your hammer over,</c>

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.240 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>straight up and down and hit the tip.</c>

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.170 line:85%
Right.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.120 line:91%
<c.yellow>Give it a good whack.
Aim the centre of your hammer</c>

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.023 line:85%
<c.yellow>at the centre of the bar.</c>

00:02:35.023 --> 00:02:38.560 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(metal clanging)</i></c>

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.110 line:91%
<c.yellow>Every time I hit,
my left hand here...</c>

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.340 line:85%
Yeah.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.930 line:91%
<c.yellow>is rotating the bar
with my fingers like this,</c>

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.720 line:85%
<c.yellow>my index finger comes around.</c>

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.553 line:85%
Yep.

00:02:48.553 --> 00:02:49.970 line:85%
<c.yellow>And every time it turns around,</c>

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.940 line:91%
<c.yellow>we lock it in at 90
degrees and hit it again.</c>

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.773 line:85%
Okay.

00:02:52.773 --> 00:02:53.940 line:85%
<c.yellow>And, we start to make a point.</c>

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.290 line:91%
We start to make a
point, yes we do, okay.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.655 line:85%
So, just take this?

00:02:57.655 --> 00:03:00.667 line:85%
Careful, yep, it's cold.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.610 line:85%
So, take that, put it there.

00:03:04.053 --> 00:03:06.150 line:91%
<c.yellow>A little further that way,
just because,</c>

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.550 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then you're going to come
back onto the anvil some more.</c>

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.760 line:91%
<c.yellow>Lift up. Up, up, up,
up, up, up, perfect.</c>

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.404 position:63% line:85%
<c.yellow>And right there, hit the end of the bar.</c>

00:03:13.404 --> 00:03:16.154 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(metal clanging)</i></c>

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.533 line:85%
<c.yellow>Brilliant.</c>

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:21.140 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, now stop for a second.</c>

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.150 line:85%
<c.yellow>Bend your knees a little bit,</c>

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.350 line:91%
<c.yellow>and get that hammer up
high and then really...</c>

00:03:26.348 --> 00:03:28.187 line:91%
I'm more worried I'm going
to miss the damn thing.

00:03:28.187 --> 00:03:31.570 line:68%
<c.yellow>Don't worry, I know the
guy that makes the anvils.</c>

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.920 line:64%
<c.yellow>He can always make another.</c>

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.280 position:59% line:64%
Oh, I know my form is terrible, but...

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.423 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's okay.</c>

00:03:37.423 --> 00:03:38.933 line:91%
I'm just happy to be hitting
the thing at this point.

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:39.766 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm going to try and
give you some feedback</c>

00:03:39.766 --> 00:03:40.960 line:85%
<c.yellow>on it for the next heat.</c>

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.580 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, let me put this camera...</c>

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.950 line:85%
Missed, completely missed.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.380 line:85%
<c.yellow>If you're happy for me to,</c>

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.873 line:91%
<c.yellow>kinda manipulate your
position a little bit?</c>

00:03:47.873 --> 00:03:49.530 line:85%
Yep, yep, go for it.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.019 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's still cold, bring
your hand closer to my hand.</c>

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:53.020 line:85%
Yup.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.040 line:85%
<c.yellow>And then, drop that shoulder some,</c>

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.890 line:91%
<c.yellow>so you can relax
a little bit like that.</c>

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:00.740 line:91%
<c.yellow>As you come with your hammer,
right here,</c>

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.990 line:91%
<c.yellow>there's a really big gap between
your elbow and your body.</c>

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.020 line:85%
<c.yellow>I'd like to close that up.</c>

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.330 line:91%
<c.yellow>So, if you can bring your
body in a little closer</c>

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.828 line:85%
<c.yellow>to the anvil like this.</c>

00:04:08.828 --> 00:04:09.661 line:85%
Yep.

00:04:09.661 --> 00:04:11.470 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>And, scrunch down a little bit more.</c>

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.060 line:91%
<c.yellow>You want to think
about having that elbow</c>

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.480 line:91%
<c.yellow>in just a little tighter
as you hit,</c>

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.940 line:85%
<c.yellow>and everything closer in,</c>

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:20.510 line:91%
<c.yellow>means that you have
a smaller moment arm.</c>

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.100 position:61% line:85%
<c.yellow>And, so you've got a little more power.</c>

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.330 line:91%
<c.yellow>So, it's better to be close in
when you're hitting the hammer.</c>

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.860 line:85%
<c.yellow>And then, now, lift that hammer up</c>

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.569 line:85%
<c.yellow>like you want to take a swing.</c>

00:04:27.569 --> 00:04:28.402 line:85%
Yeah.

00:04:28.402 --> 00:04:29.463 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's pretty good.</c>

00:04:30.802 --> 00:04:33.330 line:85%
<c.yellow>There we go, perfect.</c>

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.703 line:85%
<c.yellow>And, that'll be more like it.</c>

00:04:34.703 --> 00:04:37.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>That hammer wants to come
quite close to your head.</c>

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.580 line:85%
Yes, it does.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.130 line:85%
I'm not sure how I feel about that!

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.050 line:85%
<c.yellow>There we go.</c>

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.883 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's, that's much more like it.</c>

00:04:42.883 --> 00:04:45.081 line:91%
<c.yellow>The next heat be a much
more fun operation for you.</c>

00:04:45.081 --> 00:04:46.120 line:85%
All right, so, this goes back in?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.773 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yep, straight back in the fire.</c>

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.506 line:91%
The idea of hitting with any
precision is, that's still,

00:04:53.506 --> 00:04:54.656 line:85%
there we go, all right.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.640 line:68%
<c.yellow>Lift up with your left
hand, that's perfect.</c>

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.150 line:68%
<c.yellow>And, keep that, even
though you're tilting it,</c>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.900 line:64%
<c.yellow>keep the hammer close to your head.</c>

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.490 line:64%
<c.yellow>There we go.</c>

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:09.040 line:68%
<c.yellow>You've already got more
force on the blows.</c>

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.500 line:68%
Yeah, I'm starting to get
a little more confident,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.833 line:68%
which is probably
going to backfire on me.

00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:14.720 line:64%
<c.yellow>No, no, it won't.</c>

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.020 line:68%
<c.yellow>Nothing bad will happen
from hitting too hard.</c>

00:05:19.041 --> 00:05:20.930 line:64%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(both laugh)</i></c>

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.680 line:64%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(metal clanging)</i></c>

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.060 line:64%
<c.yellow>Let's take another heat.</c>

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.940 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow>The hotter it is, the easier it moves.</c>

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.060 line:85%
Do I get a montage now?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.200 line:85%
I feel like I get a montage.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.033 line:85%
<c.yellow>You want a montage?</c>

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.199 line:85%
Yeah, lets do a montage.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.696 line:85%
<c.yellow>Okay, I'll make you a montage.</c>

00:05:34.696 --> 00:05:37.696 align:start size:72% position:28% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>♪ (upbeat rock music)</i></c>

00:05:59.237 --> 00:06:00.087 line:85%
<c.yellow>Perfect.</c>

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.030 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's it, and can I say,
you are swinging that hammer</c>

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.850 line:91%
<c.yellow>probably 20 times as hard as
you were in the first heat.</c>

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.660 line:91%
<c.yellow>You've got so much more
speed out of that hammer swing.</c>

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.803 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's incredible, Tom.</c>

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.383 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>The steel tells you when it's right.</c>

00:06:18.383 --> 00:06:19.550 line:85%
I'm quite happy with that now.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.383 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's looking fantastic.</c>

00:06:20.383 --> 00:06:21.580 line:85%
That was wonky a minute ago.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.490 line:85%
It's still slightly wonky,

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.270 line:85%
but I'm a lot happier with that.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.290 line:91%
<c.yellow>Well, you take a
couple of minutes' break.</c>

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.329 line:85%
Yeah.

00:06:28.329 --> 00:06:29.580 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm going to get my
punch moving forwards.</c>

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.413 line:85%
Yep, okay.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.860 line:85%
<c.yellow>180 degrees and turn it over.</c>

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.070 line:85%
You make it look so easy.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.980 line:91%
<c.yellow>I do not have a
respectful response to that.</c>

00:06:51.135 --> 00:06:52.460 line:68%
No, I just suspect
a lot of people

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.120 line:68%
are going to be looking
at that and going,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.109 line:68%
oh yeah, all you have to do
is put the thing on there

00:06:56.109 --> 00:06:57.137 line:64%
and hit it and turn it and hit it.

00:06:57.137 --> 00:06:58.550 line:64%
How hard could it...?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.530 line:85%
It is very hard, is the answer.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.383 line:85%
It is extremely difficult.

00:07:06.554 --> 00:07:07.840 line:91%
<c.yellow>There we go,
and it wouldn't be the same</c>

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.530 line:85%
<c.yellow>if I didn't touch mark it.</c>

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.383 size:72% position:64% line:85%
Oh right.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.110 line:85%
<c.yellow>This end of the punch, is finished.</c>

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.420 line:85%
With your logo on it?

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.253 line:85%
<c.yellow>Sorry?</c>

00:07:21.253 --> 00:07:22.186 line:85%
With your logo on it?

00:07:22.186 --> 00:07:23.800 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yes, got my logo on it,
I wish I had letter stamps.</c>

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.029 line:91%
<c.yellow>We could stamp your name
on to the other one,</c>

00:07:26.029 --> 00:07:27.140 line:85%
<c.yellow>but I'm now going to heat it up.</c>

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.290 line:91%
<c.yellow>Cut it off and then get
back onto your drift.</c>

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.123 line:85%
Okay.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.750 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(metal clanging)</i></c>

00:07:40.166 --> 00:07:41.180 line:85%
180 degrees.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.030 line:85%
<c.yellow>Perfect.</c>

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.250 line:85%
<c.yellow>There we go.</c>

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.390 line:91%
<c.yellow>All the way up to the tip and
hit a little more at the tip.</c>

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.700 line:91%
<c.yellow>I want to make it more
like a screwdriver tip.</c>

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.200 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's it.</c>

